# The build context is the repository root, because the image needs both `web/`
# and `server/`. Everything that is neither is excluded, so that editing a
# roadmap neither invalidates a build cache nor ships a stray file.

*
!web/
!server/
# `server` depends on it by path, so it is part of the server's source whether
# or not it looks like it from here.
!telium-protocol/
# The compose file and the reference config ship inside the image so that
# `update.sh` can compare what a release wants against what the box has without
# cloning the repository onto every homeserver. They are two small text files;
# the cache invalidation they cost is the cache invalidation of editing them,
# which is exactly when a box needs to hear about them.
!deploy/compose.yml
!server/telium.example.toml

# Build output and dependencies, which the stages produce for themselves. The
# host's `target/` in particular is gigabytes of a different libc's artifacts,
# and `node_modules/` is a platform's worth of binaries the image would ignore.
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/dist-electron/
web/electron/node_modules/
web/src-tauri/target/
web/src-tauri/gen/
server/target/

.git/
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
